## Proposed repair plan
# Repair plan for failing-set

## Diagnosis

The `calc` service exposes two zero-argument accessors that are still at
their placeholder value. `services/calc/calc.go` currently reads:

```
package calc
func A() int{return 0}
func B() int{return 0}
```

The executable specification in `tests/suite/calc_test.go` (read-only for
this repair) imports `fixture/buildcodefix/services/calc` and asserts:

- `TestA` — `calc.A()` must equal `1`, otherwise it fails with `A needs one`.
- `TestB` — `calc.B()` must equal `2`, otherwise it fails with `B needs two`.

Both observed failures (`calc_test.go:3: A needs one`,
`calc_test.go:4: B needs two`) are the two assertions firing against the
placeholder zeros. There is no compile error, no missing symbol, no
wiring problem: the package name, function names, arity and `int` return
type already match what the suite imports and calls. The only defect is
the returned values. Nothing else in the repository participates in these
two tests — `services/calc/calc.go` is the single production file in the
`calc` service root declared by `docs/architecture/architecture.yaml`
(`services: - name: calc, path: services/calc`).

